1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,700
5600 K · At dusk, the harbour loses the sun first.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:07,600
KELVIN — Artificial light steps in to hold the coast.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:11,600
Every lamp rewrites the colour of the dark.

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:17,000
2100 K · Low-pressure sodium turns stone and rain to amber.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Inside one lit window, warmth becomes an island.

6
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,500
Shadows sink into Prussian blue between the pools of gold.

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,500
4200 K · Midnight shifts the spectrum—cold cyan steel and warning red.

8
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,500
In slow motion, the storm surge hangs like carved glass.

9
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:45,400
Four thousand Kelvin holds the watch until the squall breaks.

10
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:50,500
6500 K · Before sunrise, the sensors click off one by one.

11
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:55,000
Silver water remembers every colour without keeping one.

12
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:59,650
6500 K — Day returns the world to itself.
